	"hair": {
		"about": "An RL module's hl_length/hl_volume weights: clamp(shapeGain * (v - preset) / 50, -1, 1), preset = Rowan's values for rowan_shag, Mira's for mira_bun.",
		"shapeGain": 1.0,
		"detail": {
			"about": "An RL module's fine-detail level (0-100; 50 = authored, lower drops flyaway and wisp cards, 0 smooth, above 50 fades in the messy extras - keep levels 0.05-0.45 - and adds strand contrast) from the hair finish's slider position s (0 sleekest .. 100 messiest; the saved finishes sit at Swept 25, Classic 50, Tousled 75): piecewise linear through (0, 0), (sliderPresetFinish, 50) and (100, 100), rounded, sliderPresetFinish = the slider position of the module's own preset finish (Rowan Tousled for rowan_shag, Mira Swept for mira_bun), so each preset finish is the authored look. Owner decision (colour model spec revision 3, 4.7). Gives rowan_shag Swept 17 / Classic 33 / Tousled 50 and mira_bun Swept 50 / Classic 67 / Tousled 83.",
			"sliderPresetFinish": {"rowan_shag": 75, "mira_bun": 25}
		}
	},
	"colours": {
		"about": "sRGB per palette index (skin 0-9, hair colour 0-19, eyes 0-11; beards by hair colour, male only) per body sex, so the lit RL head matches what Low/Medium show for the same index: tests/integration/rl_head_colour_calibration.gd (Forward+, neutral stage light, 3 linear-light iterations): skin and eyes 2026-10-27, hair and beards 2026-10-28 for the flat painterly hair shading (rl_hair.gdshader: the diffuse no longer squares the colour; beards drawn at beard_gain), eyes again 2026-10-29 for the iris lid shade (rl_eye.gdshader, eye_style work: the table drew up to 0.012 sRGB dark; --part=eyes, each entry solved through that run's affine fit of the RL iris, which matched the old entries as measured within 0.0002). Residuals (max sRGB channel): skin 0.0002, eyes 0.0001, hair 0.001, beards 0.0005 - every hair and beard colour lands on the Low/Medium look (before the shading change: hair 0.09, the darkest colours too light; beards 0.27, light beards capped near 0.46 sRGB). Brows are the hair colour x browFromHair.",
